LOAD IMBALANCE: does scaling degrade when the block structure goes ragged?
==========================================================================
Each column is a speedup against ITS OWN t1 (unperturbed against
unperturbed, ragged against ragged). Absolute GF/s are NOT comparable
between the two -- ragged changes the shapes -- but the speedups are.
If ragged scales visibly worse, a static partition is being bound by its
unluckiest strip, and cost-weighted or dynamic assignment is worth having.
